,"p_rec":"If Medford's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Medford has set <strong class=\"sig\">12 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 85 that chance alone would give, and <strong>110 record highs</strong>, more than the 85 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (45). Medford's all-time high is 115\u00b0F, on July 20, 1946.","t_chg":"Medford's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 114 complete years: Medford's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.38\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.31 to +0.46), about +4.3\u00b0F since 1912. Medford's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.22\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.13 to +0.30), about +2.4\u00b0F since 1912.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 10 of 12 months. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Medford's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.03 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 18.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1996 (31.41 in); the driest, 2013 (8.99 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}